Upgrade procedure for unbound

Source: https://nlnetlabs.nl/downloads/unbound/unbound-VERSION.tar.gz
	(check the .sha256 and the .asc signature next to it)

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and extract the new tarball to /tmp/unbound/unbound-VERSION
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/unbound/dist, contrib/unbound,
   tag vendor/unbound/dist/VERSION).  The vendor branch carries the full
   tarball; nothing is pruned there.
3. Resolve the merge:
   - pythonmod/, testcode/, winrc/, libunbound/python/ and most of
     testdata/ are not carried in contrib/unbound.  Files the new
     release changes there show up as "deleted by us" conflicts; git rm
     them.  Files that are new upstream are added by the merge.
   - configure and config.h.in: take the upstream copies.  They are not
     used by the build.
4. Update lib/libunbound/config.h (see below).
5. Regenerate the documentation (see below).
6. Check lib/libunbound/Makefile and usr.sbin/unbound/*/Makefile against
   the new source list (midnightbsd-sources.pl can help), and compare
   with FreeBSD's import of the same version.
7. Build lib/libunbound and usr.sbin/unbound on every supported branch.
   The stable branches use an older clang and older OpenSSL.

lib/libunbound/config.h:

  config.h is maintained by hand and is the same on all supported
  branches.  When a release adds new macros, add them in autoheader
  order (compare with the new config.h.in or FreeBSD's config.h) and
  update PACKAGE_STRING, PACKAGE_VERSION and RSRC_PACKAGE_VERSION.
  Deliberate local choices:
  - It targets the OpenSSL 1.1.1 API, so one file serves branches
    with OpenSSL 1.1.1, 3.0 and 3.5: no HAVE_OPENSSL_CORE_NAMES_H,
    HAVE_OPENSSL_PARAM_BUILD_H, HAVE_EVP_MAC_CTX_SET_PARAMS or
    HAVE_SSL_GET1_PEER_CERTIFICATE; HAVE_FIPS_MODE is defined.  Only
    enable an OpenSSL function if it exists on every branch.
  - CONFCMDLINE includes --with-ssl=/usr.
  - HAVE_ATTR_NONSTRING is decided at compile time with
    __has_attribute(__nonstring__), because clang 19 lacks the
    attribute and clang 21 warns without it.
  midnightbsd-configure.sh runs configure against the base system and
  can be used to produce a reference config.h.

Generated documentation:

  doc/*.[1358] and doc/example.conf are generated from the .in
  templates.  They merge without conflicts but keep the old text, so
  regenerate them after every import:

	cd contrib/unbound/doc
	for f in example.conf libunbound.3 unbound-anchor.8 \
	    unbound-checkconf.8 unbound-control.8 unbound-host.1 \
	    unbound.8 unbound.conf.5; do
		sed -e 's,@DNSTAP_SOCKET_PATH@,,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_CHROOT_DIR@,/var/unbound,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_PIDFILE@,/var/unbound/unbound.pid,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_ROOTCERT_FILE@,/var/unbound/icannbundle.pem,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_ROOTKEY_FILE@,/var/unbound/root.key,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_RUN_DIR@,/var/unbound,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_SHARE_DIR@,/var/unbound,g' \
		    -e 's,@UNBOUND_USERNAME@,unbound,g' \
		    -e 's,@ub_conf_file@,/var/unbound/unbound.conf,g' \
		    -e 's,@ub_conf_dir@,/var/unbound,g' $f.in > $f
	done

  Check that no @VARIABLE@ is left and that new templates have not
  added variables.  dnstap/dnstap_config.h, dnscrypt/dnscrypt_config.h
  and smallapp/unbound-control-setup.sh are also generated; regenerate
  them by hand if their .in templates change.

Local patches applied on top of upstream (the same as FreeBSD's):

  - Usage strings name the local-unbound-* programs:
    smallapp/unbound-anchor.c, smallapp/unbound-checkconf.c,
    smallapp/unbound-control.c (usage()).
  - smallapp/unbound-anchor.c: const cleanup around BIO_new_mem_buf().
  - util/configlexer.lex: include config.h and "configparser.h" and
    use the ub_c_ names (ub_c_text, ub_c_error, ...) instead of yy*.
  - util/config_file.c: include "configparser.h" instead of
    "util/configparser.h" (the parser is generated in the object
    directory).
  - util/configyyrename.h: drop the yylhs ... yyrule renames (carried
    from FreeBSD; the base system yacc generates these tables as
    static).
  - util/edns.c: an "#if 0" block around #include "edns.h", carried
    from FreeBSD.
  - Generated files carried in-tree: dnscrypt/dnscrypt_config.h,
    dnstap/dnstap_config.h, smallapp/unbound-control-setup.sh.
  - smallapp/unbound-control-setup.sh.in is mode 755 in-tree (644
    upstream); content is unchanged.
  - midnightbsd-configure.sh and midnightbsd-sources.pl are local.

  These have merged cleanly so far.  If one conflicts, resolve only the
  conflicting hunk; do not take the whole file from upstream.

Notes:
  - usr.sbin/unbound/config.h is not used (lib/libunbound comes first in
    the include path).
  - usr.sbin/unbound/Makefile.inc sets MK_WERROR=no.
